   "metadata": {
    "title": "The Civil War",
    "description": "Dated, as usual, from Fort Sumter to Lee’s surrender at Appomattox; the last forces surrendered months later, and the war’s legal end came on August 20, 1866. **The cost:** the traditional count is about 620,000 soldiers dead, two-thirds of them from disease; J. David Hacker’s census-based estimate (*Civil War History*, 2011) is about 750,000, within a range of about 650,000 to 850,000. Both are estimates.",
    "tags": [
     "east",
     "west"
    ],
    "sources": [
     "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Civil_War",
